{"nodes": [{"id": "handoff", "label": "HANDOFF.md \u2014 food-DB providers, past-workout calendar, equipment variants", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "handoff_multi_provider_food_databases", "label": "Multi-provider food databases (OFF + USDA)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L18", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both providers are free and CORS-open (USDA verified access-control-allow-origin: *) and USDA complements OFF on whole foods; Nutritionix/Edamam/FatSecret were rejected because they need secret keys/OAuth, which is wrong for a no-backend app. Pluggable FoodProvider registry with zero Dexie migration thanks to the derived offId dedup key."}, {"id": "handoff_usda_fooddata_central", "label": "USDA FoodData Central (FDC)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L18", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Free external food API that complements OFF on whole foods. Branded values are per-100g, barcodes are stored as UPC-12/GTIN-14, and Foundation foods report energy under Atwater nutrients 957/958 rather than 208."}, {"id": "handoff_search_fallback_barcode_chain", "label": "Search fallback / barcode chain strategy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L48", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "User choice: text search queries OFF first and USDA only when OFF is thin (<5 results); barcode lookup tries OFF then USDA and the first hit wins."}, {"id": "handoff_anyok_error_semantics", "label": "anyOk error semantics (throw only if every provider fails)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L38", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "safeSearch swallowing all errors made a real outage show 'No results' instead of 'unreachable'; searchAcross/lookupAcross now track anyOk and rethrow only when EVERY provider errored."}, {"id": "handoff_gtin_canonicalization", "label": "GTIN canonicalization (strip leading zeros)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L37", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "FDC stores UPC-12/GTIN-14 while the zxing scanner yields EAN-13, so an exact-string gtin compare never matched; canonicalGtin strips leading zeros on both sides."}, {"id": "handoff_usda_energy_nutrient_fallback", "label": "USDA energy nutrient fallback (208 \u2192 957 \u2192 958 \u2192 kJ 268)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L36", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Foundation foods report energy under Atwater nutrients 957/958, not 208 (verified against the live API), so using 208 alone silently dropped every whole food. Try 208 \u2192 957 \u2192 958 \u2192 kJ 268/4.184, filtering unitName==='KCAL'."}, {"id": "handoff_food_dedup_gap", "label": "Food dedup gap: USDA branded search vs OFF (UPC-12 vs EAN-13)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L31", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Accepted low-severity limitation: the same product found via USDA branded search and via OFF can save as two rows when barcode formats differ; scoped out because the scan path already dedups via canonicalGtin."}, {"id": "handoff_past_workout_calendar_edit", "label": "Past-workout calendar + editing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L19", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "User choice: edits rescore the session and apply the rank delta so the score stays consistent with edited data, while achievements/quests only add, never revoke. Review fixes: dayFactor/streak are carried from the stored event (recomputing quartered the day's primary session \u2014 HIGH), the rank delta is atomic (re-read inside the transaction) with double-tap guards, a date move shifts every set's completedAt, and finish + rescore both bucket scoreEvent.date by startedAt. Edits write synced tables without withSyncTrackingSuspended because they are real user data."}, {"id": "handoff_rescore_rank_drift", "label": "Rescore rank drift (accepted limitation)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L28", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Editing an old session's e1RM/volume upward can leave a later session's PR bonus in place, so rank drifts above a from-scratch recompute (bounded by prBonusCap); the rank clamp at 0 can drift after a large downward edit. Fixing it would need a season-wide recompute subsystem, so it was accepted."}, {"id": "handoff_equipment_variants", "label": "Equipment variants (equipment on Exercise)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L20", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Variants-as-exercises separate weight data for free because all analytics key by exerciseId, carry zero risk to the scoring engine and match the seed catalog's existing variant exercises. Per-set SetRow.equipment was rejected: it would touch every weight/PR/progression/chart/briefing path and need a new index plus backfill. Switching gear means picking a different variant."}, {"id": "handoff_adversarial_review", "label": "Adversarial review workflow", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both feature batches were adversarially reviewed by a workflow (task wfi2iqdh7, scripts review-past-workout-equipment-*.js) and confirmed findings were fixed most-severe first. Lesson: build the shared prompt CONTEXT with [...].join('\\n') and never use backticks inside agent() prompt strings (template-literal parse error)."}], "edges": [{"source": "handoff", "target": "routemap", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L9", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "handoff", "target": "claude", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L9", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "handoff", "target": "claude_routemap_first_rule", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L9", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "handoff", "target": "routemap_maintenance_rule", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L9", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "handoff", "target": "routemap_invariants", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L9", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "handoff", "target": "routemap_ai_workout_coach", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L17", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "handoff", "target": "routemap_ai_diet_coach", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L17", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "handoff", "target": "handoff_multi_provider_food_databases", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "HANDOFF.md", "source_location": "L18", "weight": 1.0}, {"so